trix . C ( 2 ) through C ( N ) should contain the subdiagonal . On output , C is destroyed . D REAL ( N ) is the diagonal of the tridiagonal matrix . On output , D is destroyed . E REAL ( N ) is the superdiagonal of the tridiagonal matrix . E ( 1 ) through E ( N - 1 ) should contain the superdiagonal . On output , E is destroyed . B REAL ( N ) is the right hand side vector . On Return B is the solution vector . INFO INTEGER = 0 normal value . = K if the K - th element of the diagonal becomes exactly zero . The subroutine returns when this is detected . REFERENCES  J. J. Dongarra, J. R. Bunch, C. B. Moler, and G. W.\n                 Stewart, LINPACK Users' Guide, SIAM, 1979. ROUTINES CALLED  (NONE) REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   780814  DATE WRITTEN\n   890831  Modified array declarations.  (WRB)\n   890831  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   900326  Removed duplicate information from DESCRIPTION section.\n           (WRB)\n   920501  Reformatted the REFERENCES section.  (WRB) END PROLOGUE  SGTSL Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: N real :: C (*) real :: D (*) real :: E (*) real :: B (*) integer :: INFO","tags":"","url":"proc/sgtsl.html"},{"title":"ELPH_databases_IO_freqs – Yambo","text":"subroutine ELPH_databases_IO_freqs(ph_file, n_q, q_pt, ph_freqs) Uses pars UNITS D_lattice Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=schlen), intent(in) :: ph_file integer, intent(inout) :: n_q real(kind=SP), intent(out), optional :: q_pt (n_q,3) real(kind=SP), intent(out), optional :: ph_freqs (3*n_atoms,n_q)","tags":"","url":"proc/elph_databases_io_freqs.html"},{"title":"V_Hartree – Yambo","text":"subroutine V_Hartree(rho, vhr) Uses R_lattice D_lattice pars QP_m timing_m FFT_m electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=SP), intent(in) :: rho (fft_size) real(kind=SP), intent(out) :: vhr (fft_size,n_spin)","tags":"","url":"proc/v_hartree.html"},{"title":"X_