 – Yambo","text":"subroutine ERMSG(SUBNAM, INDIC, LEVEL, MSG, FLAG) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*) :: SUBNAM integer :: INDIC 1995-11-22 ERMSG  Krogh Got rid of multiple entries.\n1995-09-15 ERMSG  Krogh Remove '0' in format.\n1994-11-11 ERMSG  Krogh   Declared all vars.\n1992-10-20 ERMSG  WV Snyder  added ERLSET, ERLGET\n1985-09-25 ERMSG  Lawson  Initial code. integer :: LEVEL 1995-11-22 ERMSG  Krogh Got rid of multiple entries.\n1995-09-15 ERMSG  Krogh Remove '0' in format.\n1994-11-11 ERMSG  Krogh   Declared all vars.\n1992-10-20 ERMSG  WV Snyder  added ERLSET, ERLGET\n1985-09-25 ERMSG  Lawson  Initial code. character(len=*) :: MSG character(len=1) :: FLAG Common Blocks ERFIN (subroutine) SERV1 (subroutine) DERV1 (subroutine) ERMOR (subroutine) \">\n           common /M77ERR/ Type Attributes Name Initial integer :: IDELTA integer :: IALPHA","tags":"","url":"proc/ermsg.html"},{"title":"ERMSET – Yambo","text":"subroutine ERMSET(IDEL) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: IDEL","tags":"","url":"proc/ermset.html"},{"title":"setup – Yambo","text":"subroutine setup(en, Xen, Ken, k, Xk) Uses R_lattice wave_func D_lattice stderr interfaces pars com parser_m IO_m UNITS vec_operate zeros drivers electrons C_driver IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ) :: en type( levels ) :: Xen type( levels ) :: Ken type( bz_samp ) :: k type( bz_samp ) :: Xk","tags":"","url":"proc/setup.html"},{"title":"MATRIX_transfer – Yambo","text":"subroutine MATRIX_transfer(M_in, M_bse, M, M_out, INDEX_in, INDEX_out, SND, RCV, COMM, COMM_name) Uses parallel_m matrix D_lattice pars X_m timing_m BS interfaces Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( PAR_matrix ), optional :: M_in type( BS_block ), optional :: M_bse (:) complex(kind=SP), optional :: M (:,:) type( PAR_matrix ), optional :: M_out integer, optional :: INDEX_in integer, optional :: INDEX_out logical, optional :: SND logical, optional :: RCV type( yMPI_comm ), optional :: COMM character(len=*), optional :: COMM_name","tags":"","url":"proc/matrix_transfer.html"},{"title":"DQELG – Yambo","text":"subroutine DQELG(N, EPSTAB, RESULT, ABSERR, RES3LA, NRES) BEGIN PROLOGUE  DQELG SUBSIDIARY PURPOSE  The routine determines the limit of a given sequence of\n            approximations, by means of the Epsilon algorithm of\n            P.Wynn. An estimate of the absolute error is also given.\n            The condensed Epsilon table is computed. Only those\n            elements needed for the computation of the next diagonal\n            are preserved. LIBRARY   SLATEC TYPE      DOUBLE PRECISION (QELG-S, DQELG-D) KEYWORDS  CONVERGENCE ACCELERATION, EPSILON ALGORITHM, EXTRAPOLATION AUTHOR  Piessens, Robert\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven\n           de Doncker, Elise\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven DESCRIPTION Epsilon algorithm\n       Standard fortran subroutine\n       Double precision version\n\n       PARAMETERS\n          N      - Integer\n                   EPSTAB(N) contains the new element in the\n                   first column of the epsilon table.\n\n          EPSTAB - Double precision\n                   Vector of dimension 52 containing the elements\n                   of the two lower diagonals of the triangular\n                   epsilon table. The elements are numbered\n                   starting at the right-hand corner of the\n                   triangle.\n\n          RESULT - Double precision\n                   Resulting approximation to the integral\n\n          ABSERR - Double precision\n                   Estimate of the absolute error computed from\n                   RESULT and the 3 previous results\n\n          RES3LA - Double precision\n                   Vector of dimension 3 containing the last 3\n                   results\n\n          NRES   - Integer\n                   Number of calls to the routine\n                   (should be zero at first call) SEE ALSO  DQAGIE, DQAGOE, DQAGPE, DQAGSE ROUTINES CALLED  D1MACH REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   800101  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   900328  Added TYPE section.  (WRB) END PROLOGUE  DQELG **FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  DQELG Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: N double precision, dimension(52) :: EPSTAB double precision :: RESULT double precision :: ABSERR double precision, dimension(3) :: RES3LA integer :: NRES","tags":"","url":"proc/dqelg.html"},{"title":"Dipole_orb_magn_forCD – Yambo","text":"subroutine Dipole_orb_magn_forCD(Xen, Xk, Dip) Uses parallel_m R_lattice pars DIPOLES timing_m vec_operate LIVE_t electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ), intent(in) :: Xen type( bz_samp ), intent(in) :: Xk type( DIPOLE_t ), intent(inout) :: Dip","tags":"","url":"proc/dipole_orb_magn_forcd.html"},{"title":"ELPH_Sigma_c – Yambo","text":"subroutine ELPH_Sigma_c(en, k, q, qp) Uses parallel_m R_lattice ELPH interpolate com parser_m QP_m parallel_int ALLOC interfaces stderr IO_int D_lattice pars frequency QP_CTL_m IO_m UNITS timing_m drivers LIVE_t electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ) :: en type( bz_samp ) :: k type( bz_samp ) :: q type( QP_t ) :: qp","tags":"","url":"proc/elph_sigma_c.html"},{"title":"ylmr2 – Yambo","text":"subroutine ylmr2(lmax2, ng, g, gg, ylm) Uses constants kinds Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: lmax2 integer, intent(in) :: ng real(kind=DP), intent(in) :: g (3,ng) real(kind=DP), intent(in) :: gg (ng) real(kind=DP), intent(out) :: ylm (ng,lmax2)","tags":"","url":"proc/ylmr2.html"},{"title":"RT_time_step_update – Yambo","text":"subroutine RT_time_step_update(E) Uses RT_control parallel_m RT_output_m stderr pars com UNITS RT_lifetimes parallel_int electrons real_time interfaces IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ) :: E","tags":"","url":"proc/rt_time_step_update.html"},{"title":"QK15 – Yambo","text":"subroutine QK15(F, A, B, RESULT, ABSERR, RESABS, RESASC) BEGIN PROLOGUE  QK15 PURPOSE  To compute I = Integral of F over (A,B), with error\n                           estimate\n                       J = integral of ABS(F) over (A,B) LIBRARY   SLATEC (QUADPACK) CATEGORY  H2A1A2 TYPE      SINGLE PRECISION (QK15-S, DQK15-D) KEYWORDS  15-POINT GAUSS-KRONROD RULES, QUADPACK, QUADRATURE AUTHOR  Piessens, Robert\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven\n           de Doncker, Elise\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven DESCRIPTION Integration rules Standard fortran subroutine Real version PARAMETERS ON ENTRY F - Real Function subprogram defining the integrand FUNCTION F ( X ) . The actual name for F needs to be Declared E X T E R N A L in the calling program . A - Real Lower limit of integration B - Real Upper limit of integration ON RETURN RESULT - Real Approximation to the integral I Result is computed by applying the 15 - POINT KRONROD RULE ( RESK ) obtained by optimal addition of abscissae to the 7 - POINT GAUSS RULE ( RESG ) . ABSERR - Real Estimate of the modulus of the absolute error , which should not exceed ABS ( I - RESULT ) RESABS - Real Approximation to the integral J RESASC - Real Approximation to the integral of ABS ( F - I / ( B - A )) over ( A , B ) REFERENCES  (NONE) ROUTINES CALLED  R1MACH REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   800101  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB) END PROLOGUE  QK15 **FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  QK15 Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real :: F real :: A real :: B real :: RESULT real :: ABSERR real :: RESABS real :: RESASC","tags":"","url":"proc/qk15.html"},{"title":"initactivate – Yambo","text":"subroutine initactivate(mode, names) Uses it_tools it_m Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: mode character(len=*) :: names","tags":"","url":"proc/initactivate.html"},{"title":"DQC25F – Yambo","text":"subroutine DQC25F(F, A, B, OMEGA, INTEGR, NRMOM, MAXP1, KSAVE, RESULT, ABSERR, NEVAL, RESABS, RESASC, MOMCOM, CHEBMO) BEGIN PROLOGUE  DQC25F PURPOSE  To compute the integral I=Integral of F(X) over (A,B)\n            Where W(X) = COS(OMEGA X) or W(X)=SIN(OMEGA X) and to\n            compute J = Integral of ABS(F) over (A,B). For small value\n            of OMEGA or small intervals (A,B) the 15-point GAUSS-KRONRO\n            Rule is used. Otherwise a generalized CLENSHAW-CURTIS\n            method is used. LIBRARY   SLATEC (QUADPACK) CATEGORY  H2A2A2 TYPE      DOUBLE PRECISION (QC25F-S, DQC25F-D) KEYWORDS  CLENSHAW-CURTIS METHOD, GAUSS-KRONROD RULES,\n             INTEGRATION RULES FOR FUNCTIONS WITH COS OR SIN FACTOR,\n             QUADPACK, QUADRATURE AUTHOR  Piessens, Robert\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven\n           de Doncker, Elise\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven DESCRIPTION Integration rules for functions with COS or SIN factor Standard fortran subroutine Double precision version PARAMETERS ON ENTRY F - Double precision Function subprogram defining the integrand function F ( X ). The actual name for F needs to be declared E X T E R N A L in the calling program . A - Double precision Lower limit of integration B - Double precision Upper limit of integration OMEGA - Double precision Parameter in the WEIGHT function INTEGR - Integer Indicates which WEIGHT function is to be used INTEGR = 1 W ( X ) = COS ( OMEGA * X ) INTEGR = 2 W ( X ) = SIN ( OMEGA * X ) NRMOM - Integer The length of interval ( A , B ) is equal to the length of the original integration interval divided by 2 ** NRMOM ( we suppose that the routine is used in an adaptive integration process , otherwise set NRMOM = 0 ). NRMOM must be zero at the first call . MAXP1 - Integer Gives an upper bound on the number of Chebyshev moments which can be stored , i . e . for the intervals of lengths ABS ( BB - AA ) * 2 ** ( - L ), L = 0 , 1 , 2 , ..., MAXP1 - 2. KSAVE - Integer Key which is one when the moments for the current interval have been computed ON RETURN RESULT - Double precision Approximation to the integral I ABSERR - Double precision Estimate of the modulus of the absolute error , which should equal or exceed ABS ( I - RESULT ) NEVAL - Integer Number of integrand evaluations RESABS - Double precision Approximation to the integral J RESASC - Double precision Approximation to the integral of ABS ( F - I / ( B - A )) ON ENTRY AND RETURN MOMCOM - Integer For each interval length we need to compute the Chebyshev moments . MOMCOM counts the number of intervals for which these moments have already been computed . If NRMOM . LT . MOMCOM or KSAVE = 1 , the Chebyshev moments for the interval ( A , B ) have already been computed and stored , otherwise we compute them and we increase MOMCOM . CHEBMO - Double precision Array of dimension at least ( MAXP1 , 25 ) containing the modified Chebyshev moments for the first MOMCOM MOMCOM interval lengths ...................................................................... REFERENCES  (NONE) ROUTINES CALLED  D1MACH, DGTSL, DQCHEB, DQK15W, DQWGTF REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   810101  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB) END PROLOGUE  DQC25F **FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  DQC25F Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real :: F double precision :: A double precision :: B double precision :: OMEGA integer :: INTEGR integer :: NRMOM integer :: MAXP1 integer :: KSAVE double precision :: RESULT double precision :: ABSERR integer :: NEVAL double precision :: RESABS double precision :: RESASC integer :: MOMCOM double precision, dimension(maxp1,25) :: CHEBMO","tags":"","url":"proc/dqc25f.html"},{"title":"K_diago_driver – Yambo","text":"subroutine K_diago_driver(iq, W, X_static) Uses stderr linear_algebra pars com X_m frequency IO_m parser_m BS_solvers timing_m PHOTOLUM BS LIVE_t electrons MAGNONS interfaces IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: iq type( w_samp ) :: W type( X_t ), intent(in) :: X_static","tags":"","url":"proc/k_diago_driver.html"},{"title":"COLLISIONS_compress – Yambo","text":"subroutine COLLISIONS_compress(COLL) Uses pars R_lattice collision_ext Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( COLLISIONS_element ), intent(inout) :: COLL","tags":"","url":"proc/collisions_compress.html"},{"title":"IO_make_directories – Yambo","text":"subroutine IO_make_directories(what) Uses parallel_m IO_m com Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*) :: what","tags":"","url":"proc/io_make_directories.html"},{"title":"plot_check_and_launch – Yambo","text":"subroutine plot_check_and_launch(check_only) Uses D_lattice pars parser_m YPPm vec_operate Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical :: check_only","tags":"","url":"proc/plot_check_and_launch.html"},{"title":"COLLISIONS_NEQ_GW_static – Yambo","text":"subroutine COLLISIONS_NEQ_GW_static(X, Xk, E, k, q, Xw) Uses parallel_m R_lattice X_m parallel_int ALLOC interfaces plasma IO_int collision_el wave_func D_lattice pars collision_ext frequency wrapper IO_m timing_m LIVE_t electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( X_t ) :: X type( bz_samp ) :: Xk type( levels ) :: E type( bz_samp ) :: k type( bz_samp ) :: q type( w_samp ) :: Xw","tags":"","url":"proc/collisions_neq_gw_static.html"},{"title":"variables_X – Yambo","text":"function variables_X(ID, local_desc, X, EM1S_NOSOC) Uses pars X_m IO_m descriptors UNITS IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: ID type( IO_desc ) :: local_desc type( X_t ) :: X logical :: EM1S_NOSOC Return Value integer","tags":"","url":"proc/variables_x.html"},{"title":"DESC_compare – Yambo","text":"subroutine DESC_compare(D1, D2, i_err, exclude, only) Uses descriptors stderr Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( IO_desc ), intent(in) :: D1 type( IO_desc ), intent(in) :: D2 integer :: i_err (2) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: exclude character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: only","tags":"","url":"proc/desc_compare.html"},{"title":"fft_singleton – Yambo","text":"subroutine fft_singleton(a, b, ntot, n, nspan, isn) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=8) :: a (1) real(kind=8) :: b (1) integer :: ntot integer :: n integer :: nspan integer :: isn","tags":"","url":"proc/fft_singleton.html"},{"title":"RT_output – Yambo","text":"subroutine RT_output(what, VALUES, TIME, E) Uses RT_control R_lattice RT_output_m stderr interfaces pars functions com QP_m UNITS RT_lifetimes timing_m drivers fields electrons real_time C_driver Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: what real(kind=SP), intent(in), optional :: VALUES (:) real(kind=SP), intent(in), optional :: TIME real(kind=SP), intent(in), optional :: E","tags":"","url":"proc/rt_output.html"},{"title":"X_Drude – Yambo","text":"subroutine X_Drude(iq, Xen, Xk, Xw, Wd, drude_GreenF) Uses R_lattice pars com frequency X_m parser_m UNITS drivers electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: iq type( levels ), intent(in) :: Xen type( bz_samp ), intent(in) :: Xk type( w_samp ), intent(in) :: Xw complex(kind=SP), intent(inout) :: Wd complex(kind=SP), intent(out) :: drude_GreenF (Xw%n_freqs)","tags":"","url":"proc/x_drude.html"},{"title":"RT_occ_bands_interpolation – Yambo","text":"subroutine RT_occ_bands_interpolation(en, k, q, n_T_steps) Uses RT_control R_lattice interpolate YPP_interfaces stderr pars parser_m YPP_real_time UNITS YPPm LIVE_t electrons real_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ), intent(inout) :: en type( bz_samp ), intent(in) :: k type( bz_samp ), intent(in) :: q integer, intent(in) :: n_T_steps","tags":"","url":"proc/rt_occ_bands_interpolation.html"},{"title":"Check_symmetries – Yambo","text":"subroutine Check_symmetries(field_dir, field_kind) Uses D_lattice stderr matrix_operate pars com vec_operate Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=SP), intent(in) :: field_dir (3) character(len=*), intent(in) :: field_kind","tags":"","url":"proc/check_symmetries.html"},{"title":"xc_rpa_kp – Yambo","text":"subroutine xc_rpa_kp(rs, exc) Uses FFT_m pars Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=DP) :: rs (fft_size) real(kind=DP) :: exc (fft_size)","tags":"","url":"proc/xc_rpa_kp.html"},{"title":"DIPOLE_dimensions – Yambo","text":"subroutine DIPOLE_dimensions(Xen, Dip, bands, q0) Uses wave_func pars DIPOLES X_m electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ), intent(in) :: Xen type( DIPOLE_t ), intent(inout) :: Dip integer, intent(in) :: bands (2) real(kind=SP), intent(in) :: q0 (3)","tags":"","url":"proc/dipole_dimensions.html"},{"title":"INIT_barriers – Yambo","text":"subroutine INIT_barriers() Uses R_lattice D_lattice pars QP_m it_tools BS_solvers drivers BS electrons Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/init_barriers.html"},{"title":"excitons_read – Yambo","text":"subroutine excitons_read(k, Xk, en, Xen, iq, what, io_err) Uses R_lattice stderr pars X_m QP_CTL_m IO_m BS_solvers YPPm BS electrons IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( bz_samp ) :: k type( bz_samp ) :: Xk type( levels ) :: en type( levels ) :: Xen integer, intent(in) :: iq character(len=*) :: what integer, intent(out) :: io_err","tags":"","url":"proc/excitons_read.html"},{"title":"POLFIT – Yambo","text":"subroutine POLFIT(N, X, Y, W, MAXDEG, NDEG, EPS, R, IERR, A) BEGIN PROLOGUE  POLFIT PURPOSE  Fit discrete data in a least squares sense by polynomials\n            in one variable. LIBRARY   SLATEC CATEGORY  K1A1A2 TYPE      SINGLE PRECISION (POLFIT-S, DPOLFT-D) KEYWORDS  CURVE FITTING, DATA FITTING, LEAST SQUARES, POLYNOMIAL FIT AUTHOR  Shampine, L. F., (SNLA)\n           Davenport, S. M., (SNLA)\n           Huddleston, R. E., (SNLL) DESCRIPTION Abstract Given a collection of points X ( I ) and a set of values Y ( I ) which correspond to some function or measurement at each of the X ( I ), subroutine POLFIT computes the weighted least - squares polynomial fits of all degrees up to some degree either specified by the user or determined by the routine . The fits thus obtained are in orthogonal polynomial form . Subroutine PVALUE may then be called to evaluate the fitted polynomials and any of their derivatives at any point . The subroutine PCOEF may be used to express the polynomial fits as powers of ( X - C ) for any specified point C . The parameters for POLFIT are Input -- N - the number of data points . The arrays X , Y and W must be dimensioned at least N ( N . GE . 1 ) . X - array of values of the independent variable . These values may appear in any order and need not all be distinct . Y - array of corresponding function values . W - array of positive values to be used as weights . If W ( 1 ) is negative , POLFIT will set all the weights to 1.0 , which means unweighted least squares error will be minimized . To minimize relative error , the user should set the weights to : W ( I ) = 1.0 / Y ( I ) ** 2 , I = 1 , ... , N . MAXDEG - maximum degree to be allowed for polynomial fit . MAXDEG may be any non - negative integer less than N . Note -- MAXDEG cannot be equal to N - 1 when a statistical test is to be used for degree selection , i . e . , when input value of EPS is negative . EPS - specifies the criterion to be used in determining the degree of fit to be computed . ( 1 ) If EPS is input negative , POLFIT chooses the degree based on a statistical F test of significance . One of three possible significance levels will be used : . 01 , . 05 or . 10. If EPS =- 1.0 , the routine will automatically select one of these levels based on the number of data points and the maximum degree to be considered . If EPS is input as -. 01 , -. 05 , or -. 10 , a significance level of . 01 , . 05 , or . 10 , respectively , will be used . ( 2 ) If EPS is set to 0. , POLFIT computes the polynomials of degrees 0 through MAXDEG . ( 3 ) If EPS is input positive , EPS is the RMS error tolerance which must be satisfied by the fitted polynomial . POLFIT will increase the degree of fit until this criterion is met or until the maximum degree is reached . Output -- NDEG - degree of the highest degree fit computed . EPS - RMS error of the polynomial of degree NDEG . R - vector of dimension at least NDEG containing values of the fit of degree NDEG at each of the X ( I ) . Except when the statistical test is used , these values are more accurate than results from subroutine PVALUE normally are . IERR - error flag with the following possible values . 1 -- indicates normal execution , i . e . , either ( 1 ) the input value of EPS was negative , and the computed polynomial fit of degree NDEG satisfies the specified F test , or ( 2 ) the input value of EPS was 0. , and the fits of all degrees up to MAXDEG are complete , or ( 3 ) the input value of EPS was positive , and the polynomial of degree NDEG satisfies the RMS error requirement . 2 -- invalid input parameter . At least one of the input parameters has an illegal value and must be corrected before POLFIT can proceed . Valid input results when the following restrictions are observed N . GE . 1 0 . LE . MAXDEG . LE . N - 1 for EPS . GE . 0. 0 . LE . MAXDEG . LE . N - 2 for EPS . LT . 0. W ( 1 ) =- 1.0 or W ( I ) . GT . 0. , I = 1 , ... , N . 3 -- cannot satisfy the RMS error requirement with a polynomial of degree no greater than MAXDEG . Best fit found is of degree MAXDEG . 4 -- cannot satisfy the test for significance using current value of MAXDEG . Statistically , the best fit found is of order NORD . ( In this case , NDEG will have one of the values : MAXDEG - 2 , MAXDEG - 1 , or MAXDEG ) . Using a higher value of MAXDEG may result in passing the test . A - work and output array having at least 3 N + 3 MAXDEG + 3 locations Note - POLFIT calculates all fits of degrees up to and including NDEG . Any or all of these fits can be evaluated or expressed as powers of ( X - C ) using PVALUE and PCOEF after just one call to POLFIT . REFERENCES  L. F. Shampine, S. M. Davenport and R. E. Huddleston,\n                 Curve fitting by polynomials in one variable, Report\n                 SLA-74-0270, Sandia Laboratories, June 1974. ROUTINES CALLED  PVALUE, XERMSG REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   740601  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   900315  CALLs to XERROR changed to CALLs to XERMSG.  (THJ)\n   920501  Reformatted the REFERENCES section.  (WRB)\n   920527  Corrected erroneous statements in DESCRIPTION.  (WRB) END PROLOGUE  POLFIT\n**FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  POLFIT Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: N real :: X real :: Y real :: W integer :: MAXDEG integer :: NDEG real :: EPS real :: R integer :: IERR real :: A","tags":"","url":"proc/polfit.html"},{"title":"SC_History – Yambo","text":"subroutine SC_History(it, E) Uses R_lattice stderr pars com SC UNITS electrons interfaces Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: it type( levels ) :: E","tags":"","url":"proc/sc_history.html"},{"title":"EPS_extend – Yambo","text":"subroutine EPS_extend(wv, nw, iw_ref, be_verbose, ordering, eps, eps_extended) Uses pars UNITS com Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name complex(kind=SP), intent(in) :: wv (nw) integer, intent(in) :: nw integer, intent(in) :: iw_ref logical, intent(in) :: be_verbose character(len=2), intent(in) :: ordering complex(kind=SP), intent(in) :: eps (nw) complex(kind=SP), intent(out) :: eps_extended (nw)","tags":"","url":"proc/eps_extend.html"},{"title":"XERHLT – Yambo","text":"subroutine XERHLT(MESSG) BEGIN PROLOGUE  XERHLT SUBSIDIARY PURPOSE  Abort program execution and print error message. LIBRARY   SLATEC (XERROR) CATEGORY  R3C TYPE      ALL (XERHLT-A) KEYWORDS  ABORT PROGRAM EXECUTION, ERROR, XERROR AUTHOR  Jones, R. E., (SNLA)\n**DESCRIPTION Abstract\n    ***Note*** machine dependent routine\n    XERHLT aborts the execution of the program.\n    The error message causing the abort is given in the calling\n    sequence, in case one needs it for printing on a dayfile,\n    for example.\n\n Description of Parameters\n    MESSG is as in XERMSG. REFERENCES  R. E. Jones and D. K. Kahaner, XERROR, the SLATEC\n                 Error-handling Package, SAND82-0800, Sandia\n                 Laboratories, 1982. ROUTINES CALLED  (NONE) REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   790801  DATE WRITTEN\n   861211  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   900206  Routine changed from user-callable to subsidiary.  (WRB)\n   900510  Changed calling sequence to delete length of character\n           and changed routine name from XERABT to XERHLT.  (RWC)\n   920501  Reformatted the REFERENCES section.  (WRB) END PROLOGUE  XERHLT Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*) :: MESSG **FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  XERHLT","tags":"","url":"proc/xerhlt.html"},{"title":"bz_samp_indexes – Yambo","text":"subroutine bz_samp_indexes(en, k, Xk, q) Uses parallel_m R_lattice matrix_operate pars com parser_m openmp IO_m LIVE_t timing_m vec_operate drivers BS parallel_int electrons IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ) :: en type( bz_samp ) :: k type( bz_samp ) :: Xk type( bz_samp ) :: q","tags":"","url":"proc/bz_samp_indexes.html"},{"title":"DBSK0E – Yambo","text":"function DBSK0E(X) BEGIN PROLOGUE  DBSK0E PURPOSE  Compute the exponentially scaled modified (hyperbolic)\n            Bessel function of the third kind of order zero. LIBRARY   SLATEC (FNLIB) CATEGORY  C10B1 TYPE      DOUBLE PRECISION (BESK0E-S, DBSK0E-D) KEYWORDS  EXPONENTIALLY SCALED, FNLIB, HYPERBOLIC BESSEL FUNCTION,\n             MODIFIED BESSEL FUNCTION, ORDER ZERO, SPECIAL FUNCTIONS,\n             THIRD KIND AUTHOR  Fullerton, W., (LANL) DESCRIPTION DBSK0E(X) computes the double precision exponentially scaled\n modified (hyperbolic) Bessel function of the third kind of\n order zero for positive double precision argument X. Series for BK0        on the interval  0.          to  4.00000E+00\n                                        with weighted error   3.08E-33\n                                         log weighted error  32.51\n                               significant figures required  32.05\n                                    decimal places required  33.11 Series for AK0        on the interval  1.25000E-01 to  5.00000E-01\n                                        with weighted error   2.85E-32\n                                         log weighted error  31.54\n                               significant figures required  30.19\n                                    decimal places required  32.33 Series for AK02       on the interval  0.          to  1.25000E-01\n                                        with weighted error   2.30E-32\n                                         log weighted error  31.64\n                               significant figures required  29.68\n                                    decimal places required  32.40 REFERENCES  (NONE) ROUTINES CALLED  D1MACH, DBESI0, DCSEVL, INITDS, XERMSG REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   770701  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   900315  CALLs to XERROR changed to CALLs to XERMSG.  (THJ) END PROLOGUE  DBSK0E\n**FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  DBSK0E Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name double precision :: X Return Value doubleprecision","tags":"","url":"proc/dbsk0e.html"},{"title":"RT_Fluence_and_PI_kind – Yambo","text":"subroutine RT_Fluence_and_PI_kind(En, i_field) Uses pars parser_m UNITS fields electrons real_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ), intent(in) :: En integer, intent(in) :: i_field","tags":"","url":"proc/rt_fluence_and_pi_kind.html"},{"title":"INIT_activate – Yambo","text":"subroutine INIT_activate() Uses stderr QP_m BS_solvers global_XC drivers Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/init_activate.html"},{"title":"RT_Field_Commensurable_Frequencies – Yambo","text":"subroutine RT_Field_Commensurable_Frequencies() Uses fields pars real_time stderr Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/rt_field_commensurable_frequencies.html"},{"title":"MEM_defaults – Yambo","text":"subroutine MEM_defaults() Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_defaults.html"},{"title":"DBSK1E – Yambo","text":"function DBSK1E(X) BEGIN PROLOGUE  DBSK1E PURPOSE  Compute the exponentially scaled modified (hyperbolic)\n            Bessel function of the third kind of order one. LIBRARY   SLATEC (FNLIB) CATEGORY  C10B1 TYPE      DOUBLE PRECISION (BESK1E-S, DBSK1E-D) KEYWORDS  EXPONENTIALLY SCALED, FNLIB, HYPERBOLIC BESSEL FUNCTION,\n             MODIFIED BESSEL FUNCTION, ORDER ONE, SPECIAL FUNCTIONS,\n             THIRD KIND AUTHOR  Fullerton, W., (LANL) DESCRIPTION DBSK1E(S) computes the double precision exponentially scaled\n modified (hyperbolic) Bessel function of the third kind of order\n one for positive double precision argument X. Series for BK1        on the interval  0.          to  4.00000E+00\n                                        with weighted error   9.16E-32\n                                         log weighted error  31.04\n                               significant figures required  30.61\n                                    decimal places required  31.64 Series for AK1        on the interval  1.25000E-01 to  5.00000E-01\n                                        with weighted error   3.07E-32\n                                         log weighted error  31.51\n                               significant figures required  30.71\n                                    decimal places required  32.30 Series for AK12       on the interval  0.          to  1.25000E-01\n                                        with weighted error   2.41E-32\n                                         log weighted error  31.62\n                               significant figures required  30.25\n                                    decimal places required  32.38 REFERENCES  (NONE) ROUTINES CALLED  D1MACH, DBESI1, DCSEVL, INITDS, XERMSG REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   770701  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   900315  CALLs to XERROR changed to CALLs to XERMSG.  (THJ) END PROLOGUE  DBSK1E\n**FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  DBSK1E Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name double precision :: X Return Value doubleprecision","tags":"","url":"proc/dbsk1e.html"},{"title":"electrons_bands – Yambo","text":"subroutine electrons_bands(Xk, Xen) Uses R_lattice interpolate YPP_interfaces D_lattice pars com parser_m QP_CTL_m UNITS YPPm electrons interfaces Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( bz_samp ), intent(inout) :: Xk type( levels ), intent(inout) :: Xen","tags":"","url":"proc/electrons_bands.html"},{"title":"G_shells_finder – Yambo","text":"subroutine G_shells_finder() Uses parallel_m R_lattice parallel_int D_lattice pars com IO_m vec_operate zeros LIVE_t IO_int Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/g_shells_finder.html"},{"title":"X_redux – Yambo","text":"subroutine X_redux(iq, what, X_par, Xw, X) Uses parallel_m R_lattice com X_m LIVE_t parallel_int interfaces stderr matrix gpu_m linear_algebra pars frequency wrapper devxlib timing_m drivers TDDFT devxlib_async This subroutine implements the Dyson equation for the polarizability (X)\nwithin the Yambo code, handling parallel/serial/SLEPc-like (SLK)\nenvironments and managing GPU/CPU resources where available. Description The routine:\n1. Accepts the independent-particle polarizability Xo in\n   parallel/serial form.\n2. Solves the Dyson equation in serial/SLK space using the chosen\n   kernel approximation (BS, ALDA, LRC).\n3. Redistributes the computed interacting polarizability X back\n   to parallel/serial form for later use. Interfaces between PAR/SER → SER/SLK, performs the solver step,\nand then transforms back SER/SLK → PAR/SER. GPU offloading is used if available (with CUDA), except when\nincompatibilities with SLK parallelization occur. Notes Kernel types supported: BS (Bethe-Salpeter kernel) ALDA (adiabatic local-density approximation) LRC (long-range correction). Uses GPU acceleration when possible. Performs collective communications across MPI pools. Parallelization Interfaces between PAR/SER and SLK pools with MATRIX_transfer . Frequency distribution handled via PARALLEL_FREQS_setup . Collective synchronization via PP_redux_wait and PP_bcast . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: iq Index of the transferred momentum (q-point). character(len=*) :: what type( PAR_matrix ) :: X_par Parallel representation of the polarizability matrix. type( w_samp ) :: Xw Frequency sampling structure. type( X_t ) :: X Final polarizability object in serial/parallel form.","tags":"","url":"proc/x_redux.html"},{"title":"X_redux_build_kernel – Yambo","text":"subroutine X_redux_build_kernel(KERNEL, Xo, Xo_rows, Xo_cols, compute_on_gpu, iq) Uses matrix R_lattice pars Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( PAR_matrix ), target :: KERNEL type( PAR_matrix ), target :: Xo integer, intent(in) :: Xo_rows (2) integer, intent(in) :: Xo_cols (2) logical, intent(in) :: compute_on_gpu integer, intent(in) :: iq","tags":"","url":"proc/x_redux_build_kernel.html"},{"title":"Berry_polarization_NEQ – Yambo","text":"subroutine Berry_polarization_NEQ(Xen, Xk, i_sp_pol, V_bands, Polarization) Uses parallel_m R_lattice D_lattice pars QP_m hamiltonian parallel_int electrons electric Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( levels ), intent(in) :: Xen type( bz_samp ), intent(in) :: Xk integer, intent(in) :: i_sp_pol complex(kind=SP), intent(in) :: V_bands (H_ref_bands(2),Xen%nbf(i_sp_pol),QP_nk) complex(kind=SP), intent(inout) :: Polarization (3)","tags":"","url":"proc/berry_polarization_neq.html"},{"title":"QP_Green_Function – Yambo","text":"subroutine QP_Green_Function(qp, E, GFdb_read_err) Uses pars com frequency QP_m UNITS electrons Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( QP_t ) :: qp type( levels ) :: E integer :: GFdb_read_err","tags":"","url":"proc/qp_green_function.html"},{"title":"QK31 – Yambo","text":"subroutine QK31(F, A, B, RESULT, ABSERR, RESABS, RESASC) BEGIN PROLOGUE  QK31 PURPOSE  To compute I = Integral of F over (A,B) with error\n                           estimate\n                       J = Integral of ABS(F) over (A,B) LIBRARY   SLATEC (QUADPACK) CATEGORY  H2A1A2 TYPE      SINGLE PRECISION (QK31-S, DQK31-D) KEYWORDS  31-POINT GAUSS-KRONROD RULES, QUADPACK, QUADRATURE AUTHOR  Piessens, Robert\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven\n           de Doncker, Elise\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven DESCRIPTION Integration rules Standard fortran subroutine Real version PARAMETERS ON ENTRY F - Real Function subprogram defining the integrand FUNCTION F ( X ) . The actual name for F needs to be Declared E X T E R N A L in the calling program . A - Real Lower limit of integration B - Real Upper limit of integration ON RETURN RESULT - Real Approximation to the integral I RESULT is computed by applying the 31 - POINT GAUSS - KRONROD RULE ( RESK ) , obtained by optimal addition of abscissae to the 15 - POINT GAUSS RULE ( RESG ) . ABSERR - Real Estimate of the modulus of the modulus , which should not exceed ABS ( I - RESULT ) RESABS - Real Approximation to the integral J RESASC - Real Approximation to the integral of ABS ( F - I / ( B - A )) over ( A , B ) REFERENCES  (NONE) ROUTINES CALLED  R1MACH REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   800101  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB) END PROLOGUE  QK31\n**FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  QK31 Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real :: F real :: A real :: B real :: RESULT real :: ABSERR real :: RESABS real :: RESASC","tags":"","url":"proc/qk31.html"},{"title":"MEM_treshold_estimate – Yambo","text":"subroutine MEM_treshold_estimate() Uses R_lattice wave_func pars UNITS y_memory electrons Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_treshold_estimate.html"},{"title":"PLASMA_parallel_setup – Yambo","text":"subroutine PLASMA_parallel_setup(EH_gas) Uses parallel_m plasma parallel_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( plasma_gas ) :: EH_gas","tags":"","url":"proc/plasma_parallel_setup.html"},{"title":"GPU_test – Yambo","text":"subroutine GPU_test(N) Uses gpu_m devxlib pars data_m iso_c_binding Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: N","tags":"","url":"proc/gpu_test.html"},{"title":"Berry_polarization_EQ – Yambo","text":"subroutine Berry_polarization_EQ(P_Berry_RED, All_S_det, en, Xk, k_map) Uses R_lattice D_lattice pars vec_operate electrons electric Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name complex(kind=SP), intent(out) :: P_Berry_RED (3) complex(kind=SP), intent(in) :: All_S_det (6,Xk%nbz) type( levels ), intent(in) :: en type( bz_samp ), intent(in) :: Xk type( bz_map ), intent(in) :: k_map","tags":"","url":"proc/berry_polarization_eq.html"},{"title":"ZGEMM_omp – Yambo","text":"subroutine ZGEMM_omp(TRANSA, TRANSB, M, N, K, ALPHA, A, LDA, B, LDB, BETA, C, LDC) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=1) :: TRANSA character(len=1) :: TRANSB integer :: M integer :: N integer :: K complex(kind=16) :: ALPHA complex(kind=16) :: A (LDA,*) integer :: LDA complex(kind=16) :: B (LDB,*) integer :: LDB complex(kind=16) :: BETA complex(kind=16) :: C (LDC,*) integer :: LDC","tags":"","url":"proc/zgemm_omp.html"},{"title":"PCOEF – Yambo","text":"subroutine PCOEF(L, C, TC, A) BEGIN PROLOGUE  PCOEF PURPOSE  Convert the POLFIT coefficients to Taylor series form. LIBRARY   SLATEC CATEGORY  K1A1A2 TYPE      SINGLE PRECISION (PCOEF-S, DPCOEF-D) KEYWORDS  CURVE FITTING, DATA FITTING, LEAST SQUARES, POLYNOMIAL FIT AUTHOR  Shampine, L. F., (SNLA)\n           Davenport, S. M., (SNLA) DESCRIPTION Written BY L. F. Shampine and S. M. Davenport.\n\n Abstract\n\n POLFIT  computes the least squares polynomial fit of degree  L  as\n a sum of orthogonal polynomials.  PCOEF  changes this fit to its\n Taylor expansion about any point  C , i.e. writes the polynomial\n as a sum of powers of (X-C).  Taking  C=0.  gives the polynomial\n in powers of X, but a suitable non-zero  C  often leads to\n polynomials which are better scaled and more accurately evaluated.\n\n The parameters for  PCOEF  are\n\n INPUT --\n     L -      Indicates the degree of polynomial to be changed to\n              its Taylor expansion.  To obtain the Taylor\n              coefficients in reverse order, input  L  as the\n              negative of the degree desired.  The absolute value\n              of L  must be less than or equal to NDEG, the highest\n              degree polynomial fitted by  POLFIT .\n     C -      The point about which the Taylor expansion is to be\n              made.\n     A -      Work and output array containing values from last\n              call to  POLFIT .\n\n OUTPUT --\n     TC -     Vector containing the first LL+1 Taylor coefficients\n              where LL=ABS(L).  If  L.GT.0 , the coefficients are\n              in the usual Taylor series order, i.e.\n                P(X) = TC(1) + TC(2)*(X-C) + ... + TC(N+1)*(X-C)**N\n              If L .LT. 0, the coefficients are in reverse order,\n              i.e.\n                P(X) = TC(1)*(X-C)**N + ... + TC(N)*(X-C) + TC(N+1) REFERENCES  L. F. Shampine, S. M. Davenport and R. E. Huddleston,\n                 Curve fitting by polynomials in one variable, Report\n                 SLA-74-0270, Sandia Laboratories, June 1974. ROUTINES CALLED  PVALUE REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   740601  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB)\n   920501  Reformatted the REFERENCES section.  (WRB) END PROLOGUE  PCOEF **FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  PCOEF Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer :: L real :: C real :: TC real :: A","tags":"","url":"proc/pcoef.html"},{"title":"PARALLEL_FREQS_setup – Yambo","text":"subroutine PARALLEL_FREQS_setup(W, IND, COMM) Uses parallel_m parallel_int frequency Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( w_samp ) :: W type( PP_indexes ) :: IND type( yMPI_comm ) :: COMM","tags":"","url":"proc/parallel_freqs_setup.html"},{"title":"def_variable_bulk – Yambo","text":"subroutine def_variable_bulk(ID, VAR, VAR_ID, VAR_SZ, VAR_KIND, dim_names, par_io_kind, silent, chunksize) Uses parallel_m pars com netcdf IO_m Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: ID character(len=*), intent(in) :: VAR integer, intent(in) :: VAR_ID integer, intent(in) :: VAR_SZ (:) integer, intent(in) :: VAR_KIND character(len=schlen), intent(in), optional :: dim_names (:) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: par_io_kind logical, intent(in), optional :: silent integer, intent(in), optional :: chunksize (:)","tags":"","url":"proc/def_variable_bulk.html"},{"title":"COLLISIONS_load – Yambo","text":"subroutine COLLISIONS_load(CHECK_EXISTENCE_ONLY) Uses parallel_m plasma R_lattice COLL_interfaces stderr pars collision_ext com QP_m IO_m global_XC timing_m drivers hamiltonian LIVE_t IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical :: CHECK_EXISTENCE_ONLY","tags":"","url":"proc/collisions_load.html"},{"title":"cutoff_sphere – Yambo","text":"subroutine cutoff_sphere() Uses pars R_lattice wave_func Arguments None","tags":"","url":"proc/cutoff_sphere.html"},{"title":"DQK15W – Yambo","text":"subroutine DQK15W(F, W, P1, P2, P3, P4, KP, A, B, RESULT, ABSERR, RESABS, RESASC) BEGIN PROLOGUE  DQK15W PURPOSE  To compute I = Integral of F W over (A,B), with error\n                           estimate\n                       J = Integral of ABS(F W) over (A,B) LIBRARY   SLATEC (QUADPACK) CATEGORY  H2A2A2 TYPE      DOUBLE PRECISION (QK15W-S, DQK15W-D) KEYWORDS  15-POINT GAUSS-KRONROD RULES, QUADPACK, QUADRATURE AUTHOR  Piessens, Robert\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven\n           de Doncker, Elise\n             Applied Mathematics and Programming Division\n             K. U. Leuven DESCRIPTION Integration rules Standard fortran subroutine Double precision version PARAMETERS ON ENTRY F - Double precision Function subprogram defining the integrand function F ( X ). The actual name for F needs to be declared E X T E R N A L in the driver program . W - Double precision Function subprogram defining the integrand WEIGHT function W ( X ). The actual name for W needs to be declared E X T E R N A L in the calling program . P1 , P2 , P3 , P4 - Double precision Parameters in the WEIGHT function KP - Integer Key for indicating the type of WEIGHT function A - Double precision Lower limit of integration B - Double precision Upper limit of integration ON RETURN RESULT - Double precision Approximation to the integral I RESULT is computed by applying the 15 - point Kronrod rule ( RESK ) obtained by optimal addition of abscissae to the 7 - point Gauss rule ( RESG ). ABSERR - Double precision Estimate of the modulus of the absolute error , which should equal or exceed ABS ( I - RESULT ) RESABS - Double precision Approximation to the integral of ABS ( F ) RESASC - Double precision Approximation to the integral of ABS ( F - I / ( B - A )) REFERENCES  (NONE) ROUTINES CALLED  D1MACH REVISION HISTORY  (YYMMDD)\n   810101  DATE WRITTEN\n   890531  Changed all specific intrinsics to generic.  (WRB)\n   890531  REVISION DATE from Version 3.2\n   891214  Prologue converted to Version 4.0 format.  (BAB) END PROLOGUE  DQK15W **FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  DQK15W Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real :: F real :: W double precision :: P1 double precision :: P2 double precision :: P3 double precision :: P4 integer :: KP double precision :: A double precision :: B double precision :: RESULT double precision :: ABSERR double precision :: RESABS double precision :: RESASC","tags":"","url":"proc/dqk15w.html"},{"title":"io_USPP_pwscf – Yambo","text":"function io_USPP_pwscf(ID) Uses pseudo D_lattice stderr pars IO_m uspp_param qe_pseudo_m electrons us uspp IO_int Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: ID Return Value integer","tags":"","url":"proc/io_uspp_pwscf.html"},{"title":"qindx_alloc – Yambo","text":"public  subroutine qindx_alloc(what) Uses parallel_m Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: what","tags":"","url":"proc/qindx_alloc.html"},{"title":"qindx_free – Yambo","text":"public  subroutine qindx_free(what) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: what","tags":"","url":"proc/qindx_free.html"},{"title":"bz_samp_FineGd_alloc – Yambo","text":"public  subroutine bz_samp_FineGd_alloc(FG, N_coarse) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( b